{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nn, mod = map(int, input().split())\n\nmemo = {}\n\ndef solve(N, k, flag):\n    key = (N, k, flag)\n    if key in memo:\n        return memo[key]\n\n    if N == 1:\n        res = -1 if flag else (1 if k < 0 else 0)\n        memo[key] = res\n        return res\n\n    inv = N * (N - 1) // 2\n\n    if k < -inv - 1:\n        res = solve(N, -inv - 1, flag)\n        memo[key] = res\n        return res\n\n    if k >= inv:\n        memo[key] = 0\n        return 0\n\n    res = 0\n    for d in range(-N + 1, N):\n        if flag and d > 0:\n            continue\n        res = (res + solve(N - 1, k - d, (d == 0) & flag) * min(N - d, d + N)) % mod\n\n    memo[key] = res\n    return res\n\nprint(solve(n, 0, 1) % mod)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <tuple>\n#include <functional>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint n, mod;\nunordered_map<long long, int> memo;\n\nlong long encode(int N, int k, int flag) {\n    return ((long long)N << 40) | ((long long)(k + 1000000000LL) << 20) | flag;\n}\n\nint solve(int N, int k, int flag) {\n    long long key = encode(N, k, flag);\n    auto it = memo.find(key);\n    if (it != memo.end()) return it->second;\n\n    if (N == 1) {\n        int res;\n        if (flag) {\n            res = -1;\n        } else {\n            res = (k < 0) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        memo[key] = res;\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    int inv = N * (N - 1) / 2;\n\n    if (k < -inv - 1) {\n        int res = solve(N, -inv - 1, flag);\n        memo[key] = res;\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    if (k >= inv) {\n        memo[key] = 0;\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    int res = 0;\n    for (int d = -N + 1; d < N; ++d) {\n        if (flag && d > 0) continue;\n        int term = solve(N - 1, k - d, (d == 0) & flag);\n        int mult = min(N - d, d + N);\n        res = (res + (long long)term * mult) % mod;\n    }\n\n    memo[key] = res;\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n\n    int result = solve(n, 0, 1) % mod;\n    cout << result << '\\n';\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.8410846e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00048101298, -0.0006056382, -0.0005684667, -1.5044966, -1.9192512e-05, -2.3841855e-07, -2.3841855e-07, -1.7899667, -1.072883e-06, -9.989239e-05, -0.0007270315, -2.3841855e-07, -0.06110897, -0.020616174, -0.018276852, -4.0531077e-06, -0.461575, -0.12710758, -0.029896786, -5.960463e-07, 0.0, -0.004085053, -0.6734914, -0.10278931, -0.0069229025, -0.0015112658, -0.12696259, -0.01425324, 0.0, -0.032691266, -0.3289155, -1.072883e-06, -1.7881378e-06, -0.12698716, -4.2915253e-06, -7.2715025e-05, -0.0020566282, -0.21512245, 0.0, -0.22029163, -0.022044733, -0.023364939, -1.072883e-06, -0.0040789987, -8.463824e-06, -1.7881378e-06, -0.20142113, -1.3589766e-05, -4.0531077e-06, -3.81469e-06, -1.2993728e-05, -0.07760725, -0.20417073, -8.856858e-05, 0.0, 